# 111blackmagic_riscv_merged.patch
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
# ---------------------
# Consolidates all RISC-V debug module fixes, performance optimizations, fault tolerance,
# and protocol enhancements (formerly patches 13, 21, 26, 89, 92, 93, 94, 95, 100, 101, 102,
# 103, 104, and RISC-V portions of 82bis, 83bis, 85bis, 105):
#
# 1. Fault tolerance on 1-wire transports (SDI / RVSWD) (patches 100, 101, 102, 103):
#    - Per riscv_fault.md F1/F2: Quiesces the abstractauto streaming pipeline before writes
#      that must not race an active command (progbuf neutralise, abstractauto=0, a0/a1 restores).
#      Saves and restores dpc around program buffer execution per RISC-V Debug Spec 3.7.
#    - Per riscv_fault.md F3: Asserts haltreq before reset is triggered and holds it across
#      ndmreset / nRST reactivation so the hart halts at the reset vector rather than running
#      startup code before halting.
#    - Per riscv_fault.md F5: Re-issues faulted memory read windows (up to 8 attempts) when
#      detected, preventing spurious section read failures.
#    - Per riscv_fault.md F5/12.6/12.8: Single-wire SDI cannot report dropped DMI transfers
#      in real time and may repeat stale data; performs two-pass consensus reading with
#      element-level fallback and end-of-transfer abstractioncs check.
#
# 2. CSR and ebreak handling (patch 104):
#    - Debug registers (dcsr 0x7b0, dpc 0x7b1, etc.) cannot be accessed via CPU instructions
#      in progbuf (triggers illegal instruction). Exempts 0x7b0..0x7bf from progbuf fallback.
#    - Enables ebreakm in dcsr during riscv_attach() and riscv_reset() and preserves it during
#      single-stepping so software breakpoints immediately halt into debug mode.
#
# 3. RV32E support (patches 93, 95):
#    - RV32E has 16 GPRs instead of 32. Vanilla code mapped GDB register 32 (PC) to x16 on
#      RV32E targets (such as CH32V003), causing E01 errors on 'load' and 'set $pc'.
#    - Fixes flashstub execution on RV32E to write to the PC register properly.
#
# 4. DMI and performance optimizations (patches 85bis, 89):
#    - Lean ADI DTM DMI path driving TAR/DRW directly without per-op RDBUFF flush + status poll.
#    - Abstractauto streaming memory read/write pipelines and sysbus autoexec support.
#
# 5. Reset & command robustness (patches 92, 94, 26):
#    - Drops RV_DM_STAT_ALL_RESET poll in riscv_reset() which caused 1-second hangs on RP2350
#      RISC-V harts that clear allhavereset upon reset.
#    - Adds a 200ms timeout to riscv_command_wait_complete() to prevent infinite lockups on disconnect.
#    - Explicitly reports errors when watchpoint allocation fails.
#
# 6. RVSWD & target metadata (patches 13, 21, 82bis, 105):
#    - Adds native RVSWD debug protocol support.
#    - Declares RISC-V flashstub hooks.
#    - Tags RISC-V architecture in target options (TOPT_ARCH_RISCV).
#    - Disables obsolete C XML target descriptions in riscv_debug.c (handled by Rust).
#
# FIX
# ---
# 1. In riscv_debug.c:
#    - Exempt 0x7b0..0x7bf debug registers from progbuf in riscv_csr_read/write.
#    - Set RV_DCSR_EBREAK_MACHINE in riscv_attach(), riscv_reset(), and riscv_halt_resume().
#    - In riscv_reset(), hold haltreq across reset and remove allhavereset polling.
#    - Add timeout to riscv_command_wait_complete().
#    - In riscv_dmi_write(), invalidate DMI caches when requested.
#
# 2. In riscv32.c:
#    - Fix GPR count on RV32E so PC (reg 32) is accessed via CSR dpc (0x7b1) rather than x16.
#    - Implement retry loop (RV_MEM_READ_RETRIES) and SDI read confirmation in riscv32_mem_read().
#    - Implement pipeline quiesce and dpc save/restore in progbuf memory read/write routines.
#
# 3. In riscv_adi_dtm.c:
#    - Implement lean direct DMI access driving TAR/DRW without per-op status polling.
#
# 4. In riscv_debug.h:
#    - Add shared RV_DM_ABSTRACTAUTO, RV_HART_FLAG_MEMORY_ABSTAUTO, and timing/status definitions.
#
